I fixed most of #1114 but not all of it, so I titled the commit "Part of #1114" instead of "Fixes". The ticket stays open for the rest.

What's fixed: yoyo -p --print-system-prompt now sends --print-system-prompt as the prompt instead of printing the system prompt, and the "looks like another flag" warning still shows. yoyo --system --yes hi no longer turns on auto-approve; --yes is just the system prompt text there.

How: yesterday's fix made cli_config::has_option skip the word right after a flag that takes a value. All the on/off flag checks in cli.rs now go through it. The five checks that read the next word (--output-format, --cost-warn, --system-file, --thinking, --context-strategy) go through a new option_position, which walks the arguments the same way and returns the flag's position. That's 34 of 34 checks, counted by grep rather than taken from the issue's estimate of 31. cli.rs shrank from 7872 to 7863 lines, and I updated its entry in tests/module_size.rs.

What's still broken: flags that take a value are still picked up from another flag's value slot. On the built binary, yoyo --system --model claude-zzz -p hi warns about the flag-like value and then runs on model claude-zzz. These lookups go through dispatch_sub::flag_value (54 callers, shared with subcommand parsing), collect_repeatable_flag and resolve_numeric_setting. That needs its own fix, so I posted the repro and the open question on #1114.

Tests:
• tests/flag_value_slot.rs runs the real binary against a local stub server, with the key-scrubbing helper copied from unknown_flag_refusal.rs. It covers four cases: -p --print-system-prompt sends the text; bare --print-system-prompt still prints; --system --print-system-prompt --print-system-prompt prints a system prompt that is the literal text; and -- --print-system-prompt sends it.
• --yes has no visible effect without a real model turn, so src/cli_flag_slot_tests.rs checks the parsed config directly. It has 9 rows, both where auto-approve should stay off and where it should come on.
• I broke two of the fixes on purpose, one at a time, and each made the matching test fail by name. Both are restored and no sabotage markers are left.
• cargo fmt --check, clippy -D warnings and the full cargo test all pass.

Docs: the sentence in docs/src/usage/single-prompt.md that pointed at #1114 now says what's fixed and what's still tracked there.

One thing to watch: the harness's own commit template still says "Fixes #1114". If it adds a later commit with that title, pushing it would close the ticket while the value-flag problem is still open.
